---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="Privacy policy for Hotel Menu Guide: we collect no personal data, set no tracking cookies, and run no analytics."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: September 30, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose-guide mt-6">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This site collects nothing about you. There are no accounts, no forms that store data,
        no analytics, no advertising trackers, and no cookies beyond what your browser needs to
        load a page.
      </p>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. We don't ask for your name, email, or any personal information anywhere on this
        site. The contact page links to public social profiles; if you message us there, that
        conversation lives on that platform under its own privacy policy.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We set no cookies of our own — no tracking cookies, no advertising cookies, no preference
        cookies. (Your browser may store ordinary technical data like cached images, as it does
        for every website.)
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        We run no analytics software and serve no third-party advertising on this site. Nobody is
        building a profile of your visit here.
      </p>
      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        Our guides link to restaurants' official websites and public profiles. Once you follow one
        of those links, their privacy policies apply, not ours.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy ever changes, we'll update the date above. Given how little there is to
        change, don't hold your breath.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
